{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: report prices now round to the nearest 5 cents instead of always rounding down.\n\n**The bug:** `round_to_nickel` in `repo/pricing.py` was rounding down to the multiple of 5 below. So 23¢ showed as 20¢ instead of 25¢, and 99¢ showed as 95¢. This affected every rounded price, including the `rounded_total` in `price_summary`.\n\n**The fix:** a one-line change:\n\n```python\nreturn ((cents + 2) // 5) * 5\n```\n\nAmounts ending in 1–2 or 6–7 cents now round down, and amounts ending in 3–4 or 8–9 round up. Cents are whole numbers, so no amount is ever exactly halfway between two nickels and there's no tie to decide. Negative amounts round the same way (−23 becomes −25).\n\n**Checks:** both existing tests pass. I also spot-checked amounts from −23 to 100, and they all matched the examples in the function's own description. One thing to know: `old_round`, the old rounding for v1 receipts, just calls this function, so it picks up the fix too.\n\nI didn't touch the unrelated TODOs in `format.py` and `rows.py`."}]},"session_id":"f42bd792-a8d2-4f61-96b2-0e70a88badcd"}
